   "source": [
    "# Population Density vs Energy Access Analysis for Zambia\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook performs a geospatial analysis of population density versus energy access in Zambia by examining the proximity of substations within a 10km buffer zone.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Analysis Overview\n",
    "1. **Population Density Layer**: WorldPop population density data for Zambia\n",
    "2. **Transmission Lines Layer**: OpenStreetMap transmission lines with voltage-based color coding\n",
    "3. **Substations Layer**: OpenStreetMap substations with 10km buffer zones\n",
    "4. **Layered Visualization**: Combined analysis with light theme and good contrast\n",
    "\n",
    "## Data Sources\n",
    "- **WorldPop**: Population density raster data\n",
    "- **OpenStreetMap**: Transmission infrastructure via Overpass API"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Import required libraries\n",
    "import os\n",
    "import requests\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import geopandas as gpd\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import matplotlib.patches as patches\n",
    "from matplotlib.colors import LinearSegmentedColormap, Normalize\n",
    "import rasterio\n",
    "from rasterio.plot import show\n",
    "from rasterio.mask import mask\n",
    "import overpy\n",
    "from shapely.geometry import Point, Polygon, LineString\n",
    "import contextily as ctx\n",
    "import folium\n",
    "from PIL import Image\n",
    "import warnings\n",
    "warnings.filterwarnings('ignore')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Set matplotlib style for light theme with good contrast\n",
    "plt.style.use('default')\n",
    "plt.rcParams['figure.facecolor'] = 'white'\n",
    "plt.rcParams['axes.facecolor'] = 'white'\n",
    "plt.rcParams['axes.edgecolor'] = 'black'\n",
    "plt.rcParams['axes.linewidth'] = 1.2\n",
    "plt.rcParams['xtick.color'] = 'black'\n",
    "plt.rcParams['ytick.color'] = 'black'\n",
    "plt.rcParams['text.color'] = 'black'\n",
    "plt.rcParams['font.size'] = 11\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Libraries imported successfully!\")"
   ]
